{"path": "src/networking.c", "lines": "200-350 of 3154", "content": "200:  *
201:  * If the client should receive new data (normal clients will) the function
202:  * returns C_OK, and make sure to install the write handler in our event
203:  * loop so that when the socket is writable new data gets written.
204:  *
205:  * If the client should not receive new data, because it is a fake client
206:  * (used to load AOF in memory), a master or because the setup of the write
207:  * handler failed, the function returns C_ERR.
208:  *
209:  * The function may return C_OK without actually installing the write
210:  * event handler in the following cases:
211:  *
212:  * 1) The event handler should already be installed since the output buffer
213:  *    already contains something.
214:  * 2) The client is a slave but not yet online, so we want to just accumulate
215:  *    writes in the buffer but not actually sending them yet.
216:  *
217:  * Typically gets called every time a reply is built, before adding more
218:  * data to the clients output buffers. If the function returns C_ERR no
219:  * data should be appended to the output buffers. */
220: int prepareClientToWrite(client *c) {
221:     /* If it's the Lua client we always return ok without installing any
222:      * handler since there is no socket at all. */
223:     if (c->flags & (CLIENT_LUA|CLIENT_MODULE)) return C_OK;
224: 
225:     /* CLIENT REPLY OFF / SKIP handling: don't send replies. */
226:     if (c->flags & (CLIENT_REPLY_OFF|CLIENT_REPLY_SKIP)) return C_ERR;
227: 
228:     /* Masters don't receive replies, unless CLIENT_MASTER_FORCE_REPLY flag
229:      * is set. */
230:     if ((c->flags & CLIENT_MASTER) &&
231:         !(c->flags & CLIENT_MASTER_FORCE_REPLY)) return C_ERR;
232: 
233:     if (!c->conn) return C_ERR; /* Fake client for AOF loading. */
234: 
235:     /* Schedule the client to write the output buffers to the socket, unless
236:      * it should already be setup to do so (it has already pending data). */
237:     if (!clientHasPendingReplies(c)) clientInstallWriteHandler(c);
238: 
239:     /* Authorize the caller to queue in the output buffer of this client. */
240:     return C_OK;
241: }
